IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`

§ `Chapter 2 -- Attribution of acts and of liability`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 32, 33, 34, 35, 36, 37, 38.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- These are the Code's rules for who is liable for what, short of abetment
-- (Chapter 5) and criminal conspiracy (Chapter 5A). They attribute an act done by
-- several people to each of them, and they settle what counts as one act.
-- Section 39 is repealed.

§§ `Elements`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 32 to 38"
DECLARE `Joint Act Facts` HAS
    `the words of the offence refer to acts done` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a contrary intention appears from the context` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the thing in question is an illegal omission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct is a series of acts rather than a single act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conduct is a series of omissions rather than a single omission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one or more of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is not known which of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a criminal act is done by several persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act is done in furtherance of the common intention of all of them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person is one of those persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act is criminal only by reason of being done with a criminal knowledge or intention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person joins in the act with that knowledge or intention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is the causing of an effect or an attempt to cause it by an act or by an omission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the effect was caused partly by an act and partly by an omission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence is committed by means of several acts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person intentionally cooperates in the commission of the offence by doing one of those acts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `several persons are engaged or concerned in the commission of a criminal act` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Section 32 -- Words referring to acts include illegal omissions`

-- In every part of the Code, except where a contrary intention appears from the
-- context, words which refer to acts done extend also to illegal omissions.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 32"
@export Decide whether an illegal omission falls within words of the Penal Code 1871 that refer to acts done, under section 32
GIVEN j IS A `Joint Act Facts` @desc The offence wording and the conduct. An illegal omission is within words referring to acts unless a contrary intention appears from the context.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the illegal omission is within the words referring to acts` IF
        j's `the words of the offence refer to acts done`
    AND j's `the thing in question is an illegal omission`
    AND (NOT j's `a contrary intention appears from the context`)

§§ `Section 33 -- Act and omission`

-- s 33(1): "act" denotes a series of acts as well as a single act; "omission"
-- denotes a series of omissions as well as a single omission.
-- s 33(2): where a person does a series of acts, one or more of which caused a
-- certain effect, that person is regarded as having caused that effect by that
-- series even if it is not known which act in the series caused it.
-- Illustration: A gives Z small doses of poison over several days intending to kill
-- Z. Z dies of poisoning although it is not known which dose caused the death. A
-- has caused Z's death by poisoning.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 33(1)"
GIVEN j IS A `Joint Act Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the series counts as a single act or omission` IF
        j's `the conduct is a series of acts rather than a single act`
    OR  j's `the conduct is a series of omissions rather than a single omission`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 33(2)"
@export Decide whether a person caused an effect by a series of acts under Penal Code 1871 section 33(2)
GIVEN j IS A `Joint Act Facts` @desc A series of acts, one or more of which caused the effect. It does not matter that it is unknown which act in the series caused it.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person caused the effect by the series of acts` IF
        j's `the conduct is a series of acts rather than a single act`
    AND j's `one or more of the acts in the series caused the effect`

§§ `Section 34 -- Common intention`

-- When a criminal act is done by several persons in furtherance of the common
-- intention of all, each of them is liable for that act in the same manner as if
-- the act were done by him alone.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 34"
@export Decide whether a person is liable for a criminal act done by several persons in furtherance of a common intention, under Penal Code 1871 section 34
GIVEN j IS A `Joint Act Facts` @desc A criminal act done by several persons, done in furtherance of the common intention of all of them, and this person one of them.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is liable under section 34 as if he did the act alone` IF
        j's `a criminal act is done by several persons`
    AND j's `the act is done in furtherance of the common intention of all of them`
    AND j's `this person is one of those persons`

§§ `Section 35 -- Joining in an act criminal by reason of knowledge or intention`

-- Whenever an act which is criminal only by reason of its being done with a criminal
-- knowledge or intention is done by several persons, each of them who joins in the
-- act with that knowledge or intention is liable for the act in the same manner as
-- if the act were done by him alone with that knowledge or intention.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 35"
@export Decide whether a person who joins in an act criminal only by reason of knowledge or intention is liable under Penal Code 1871 section 35
GIVEN j IS A `Joint Act Facts` @desc An act criminal only by reason of the knowledge or intention with which it is done, done by several persons, and this person joining in it with that knowledge or intention.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is liable under section 35 as if he did the act alone` IF
        j's `the act is criminal only by reason of being done with a criminal knowledge or intention`
    AND j's `a criminal act is done by several persons`
    AND j's `this person is one of those persons`
    AND j's `this person joins in the act with that knowledge or intention`

§§ `Section 36 -- Effect caused partly by act and partly by omission`

-- Wherever the causing of an effect, or an attempt to cause it, by an act or by an
-- omission is an offence, the causing of that effect partly by an act and partly by
-- an omission is the same offence.
-- Illustration: A intentionally causes Z's death partly by illegally omitting to
-- give Z food and partly by beating Z. A has committed murder.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 36"
@export Decide whether an effect caused partly by act and partly by omission is the same offence under Penal Code 1871 section 36
GIVEN j IS A `Joint Act Facts` @desc An offence consisting in the causing of an effect, or an attempt to cause it, by an act or by an omission, where the effect was in fact caused by a mixture of the two.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mixed act and omission is the same offence` IF
        j's `the offence is the causing of an effect or an attempt to cause it by an act or by an omission`
    AND j's `the effect was caused partly by an act and partly by an omission`

§§ `Section 37 -- Cooperation by doing one of several acts constituting an offence`

-- When an offence is committed by means of several acts, whoever intentionally
-- cooperates in the commission of that offence by doing any one of those acts,
-- either singly or jointly with any other person, commits that offence.
-- Illustration (c) marks the limit: a successor jailer who starves a prisoner
-- without collusion with his predecessor does not cooperate with him, so the
-- predecessor is guilty only of an attempt.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 37"
@export Decide whether a person commits an offence by cooperating in one of the several acts constituting it, under Penal Code 1871 section 37
GIVEN j IS A `Joint Act Facts` @desc An offence committed by means of several acts, and this person intentionally cooperating in its commission by doing one of those acts, singly or jointly with another.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence by cooperation under section 37` IF
        j's `the offence is committed by means of several acts`
    AND j's `this person intentionally cooperates in the commission of the offence by doing one of those acts`

§§ `Section 38 -- Different offences from the same criminal act`

-- Where several persons are engaged or concerned in the commission of a criminal
-- act, they may be guilty of different offences by means of that act.
-- Illustration: A kills Z under grave provocation, so his killing is culpable
-- homicide not amounting to murder; B, not provoked and intending to kill, assists.
-- B is guilty of murder and A only of culpable homicide.
--
-- s 38 is permissive: it removes an obstacle to charging differently rather than
-- imposing a condition. It is encoded as the fact that the differing-offences
-- outcome is open, which is what the section decides.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 38"
@export Decide whether persons engaged in one criminal act may be guilty of different offences under Penal Code 1871 section 38
GIVEN j IS A `Joint Act Facts` @desc Several persons engaged or concerned in the commission of a criminal act. Their several liabilities are then assessed separately on their own fault elements and defences.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the participants may be guilty of different offences` IF
    j's `several persons are engaged or concerned in the commission of a criminal act`

§§ `Illustrations`

`blank joint act` MEANS `Joint Act Facts` WITH
    `the words of the offence refer to acts done` IS FALSE
    `a contrary intention appears from the context` IS FALSE
    `the thing in question is an illegal omission` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is a series of acts rather than a single act` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is a series of omissions rather than a single omission` IS FALSE
    `one or more of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS FALSE
    `it is not known which of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS FALSE
    `a criminal act is done by several persons` IS FALSE
    `the act is done in furtherance of the common intention of all of them` IS FALSE
    `this person is one of those persons` IS FALSE
    `the act is criminal only by reason of being done with a criminal knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `this person joins in the act with that knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `the offence is the causing of an effect or an attempt to cause it by an act or by an omission` IS FALSE
    `the effect was caused partly by an act and partly by an omission` IS FALSE
    `the offence is committed by means of several acts` IS FALSE
    `this person intentionally cooperates in the commission of the offence by doing one of those acts` IS FALSE
    `several persons are engaged or concerned in the commission of a criminal act` IS FALSE

-- s 33(2) Illustration: the doses of poison.
`poison given in doses over days` MEANS `Joint Act Facts` WITH
    `the words of the offence refer to acts done` IS TRUE
    `a contrary intention appears from the context` IS FALSE
    `the thing in question is an illegal omission` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is a series of acts rather than a single act` IS TRUE
    `the conduct is a series of omissions rather than a single omission` IS FALSE
    `one or more of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS TRUE
    `it is not known which of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS TRUE
    `a criminal act is done by several persons` IS FALSE
    `the act is done in furtherance of the common intention of all of them` IS FALSE
    `this person is one of those persons` IS FALSE
    `the act is criminal only by reason of being done with a criminal knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `this person joins in the act with that knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `the offence is the causing of an effect or an attempt to cause it by an act or by an omission` IS TRUE
    `the effect was caused partly by an act and partly by an omission` IS FALSE
    `the offence is committed by means of several acts` IS FALSE
    `this person intentionally cooperates in the commission of the offence by doing one of those acts` IS FALSE
    `several persons are engaged or concerned in the commission of a criminal act` IS FALSE

-- s 34: the common-intention robbery.
`joint act in furtherance of common intention` MEANS `Joint Act Facts` WITH
    `the words of the offence refer to acts done` IS TRUE
    `a contrary intention appears from the context` IS FALSE
    `the thing in question is an illegal omission` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is a series of acts rather than a single act` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is a series of omissions rather than a single omission` IS FALSE
    `one or more of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS FALSE
    `it is not known which of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS FALSE
    `a criminal act is done by several persons` IS TRUE
    `the act is done in furtherance of the common intention of all of them` IS TRUE
    `this person is one of those persons` IS TRUE
    `the act is criminal only by reason of being done with a criminal knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `this person joins in the act with that knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `the offence is the causing of an effect or an attempt to cause it by an act or by an omission` IS FALSE
    `the effect was caused partly by an act and partly by an omission` IS FALSE
    `the offence is committed by means of several acts` IS FALSE
    `this person intentionally cooperates in the commission of the offence by doing one of those acts` IS FALSE
    `several persons are engaged or concerned in the commission of a criminal act` IS TRUE

-- s 34 fails where the several persons act without a common intention.
`joint act without common intention` MEANS `Joint Act Facts` WITH
    `the words of the offence refer to acts done` IS TRUE
    `a contrary intention appears from the context` IS FALSE
    `the thing in question is an illegal omission` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is a series of acts rather than a single act` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is a series of omissions rather than a single omission` IS FALSE
    `one or more of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS FALSE
    `it is not known which of the acts in the series caused the effect` IS FALSE
    `a criminal act is done by several persons` IS TRUE
    `the act is done in furtherance of the common intention of all of them` IS FALSE
    `this person is one of those persons` IS TRUE
    `the act is criminal only by reason of being done with a criminal knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `this person joins in the act with that knowledge or intention` IS FALSE
    `the offence is the causing of an effect or an attempt to cause it by an act or by an omission` IS FALSE
    `the effect was caused partly by an act and partly by an omission` IS FALSE
    `the offence is committed by means of several acts` IS FALSE
    `this person intentionally cooperates in the commission of the offence by doing one of those acts` IS FALSE
    `several persons are engaged or concerned in the commission of a criminal act` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the person caused the effect by the series of acts` `poison given in doses over days`
#ASSERT `the person is liable under section 34 as if he did the act alone` `joint act in furtherance of common intention`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is liable under section 34 as if he did the act alone` `joint act without common intention`)
#ASSERT `the participants may be guilty of different offences` `joint act without common intention`
#ASSERT NOT (`the illegal omission is within the words referring to acts` `blank joint act`)
